Error [jet.UninitializedRead]: `cells` may be read before it is given a value
  --> UnfilledReferenceList.jet:9:11
    |
  9 |     print(cells[0])
    |           ^^^^^
 Why: `cells` was declared with `Type{ uninit }`, so no value is available until you write to it — this read could see garbage
 Fix: Assign `cells` on every path before reading it; a fixed list needs every slot assigned
